preConditionHook:
// PriorBarAtrTrailingStop -- Grimes A list, key PriorBarAtrTrailingStop
// (G08-16): "consider stops that limit your loss on any one day, perhaps a
// certain ATR multiple from the previous day's high, low, or closing values."
// Authored 2026-09-22 as stopOffsetAtr / atrLength inputs on
// TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold and split out as its own rule 2026-11-07,
// because the 202611 BRK and OWN templates place
// TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold, so TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold stays
// exactly as those families run it. Code otherwise unchanged. The defaults are
// Grimes's unarmed, pure-ATR form: stopOffsetAtr(1.5) is his multiple of about
// 1.5 ATR, stopOffsetTicks(0) drops the fixed tick offset, and
// armProfitDollars(0) leaves the trail unarmed -- live from the fill bar --
// because ctx.MaxPositionProfit() starts at 0 and the arming test is >=.
//
// A PRIOR-BAR TRAIL WITH AN ATR OFFSET: a close beyond the PRIOR bar's adverse
// extreme by stopOffsetAtr ATRs (plus stopOffsetTicks ticks) takes the trade
// off. A tick offset is FIXED and does not scale, so the day's allowed adverse
// move shrinks in ATR terms as volatility rises; the ATR term is what Grimes
// actually asks for. The ADVERSE extreme (the prior bar's low for a long) is
// the anchor; the high and close anchors Grimes also lists are recorded, not
// given an input. THE TWO OFFSETS ARE ADDITIVE. At stopOffsetAtr 0 this fires
// exactly where TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold does, at whatever
// armProfitDollars and stopOffsetTicks it is given.
//
// THE OPTIONAL ARMING GATE is TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold's: with
// armProfitDollars above 0 the trail does not arm until the trade has shown
// that much open profit, and before that the wider initial stop (a separate
// placement) stands alone.
//
// R29-14 states this as a GATE on other tightening rules -- "do not tighten
// until about four ticks of profit" -- which the pane system cannot express,
// since exits are ORed and one exit cannot condition another. The only
// mechanizable shape is the single armed-trail exit written here, the same
// recast NumBarsIfProfitable makes for the profit-gated time stop.
//
// ARMING IS ctx.MaxPositionProfit(), NOT A HAND-ROLLED FLAG: it is VERIFIED as
// the INTRABAR peak, net of the entry side's costs, starting at 0 per position
// and restarting through a reversal, so it is already the once-true-per-position
// latch this rule needs and nothing has to be reset. armProfitDollars is
// CURRENCY, not ticks -- the source's four ticks is a per-symbol statement of
// the same idea, and the dollar form is the corpus's threshold currency.
//
// The tick offset IS ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is
// written division-first, stopOffsetTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()),
// computed once per bar into a local since both are per-symbol constants.
//
// SIDES ARE MIRRORED, correcting the merged `same`: the long reads the prior
// bar's low and the short the prior bar's high, which is directional. The same
// correction BreakevenStop and BreakevenExitAfterAdverseExcursion needed.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope
// declaration, so the hooks survive a double placement.
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, not the built-in it
// resembles: seeded with a full N-term sum on the first calculated bar and
// again whenever the length changes, and thereafter updated as TWO
// statements -- EL
// evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right and folding it to S += in - out
// rounds differently. Ported from AtrProfitTarget / SwingPivotTarget. Read
// once per bar into a local, never inside a condition: EL does not
// short-circuit and/or, so an accumulator in a condition would advance on
// every bar in EL and only on some bars here. The local counter is atrLen,
// not atrLength: atrLength is this rule's INPUT.
//
// Deepest bar touched: atrLength + 1, at every stopOffsetAtr: the
// accumulator is read on every bar.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
armed = el_ge(ctx.MaxPositionProfit(), armProfitDollars);
if (atrLen != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLength; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLength;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atrVal = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
